criteria:
Inclusion criteria:
1. Male or female patients aged ≥18 years
2. Histological confirmation of rectal adenocarcinoma
3. Patients undergoing neoadjuvant treatment for locally advanced tumor of the  rectum with confirmed major clinical response after neoadjuvant treatment
4. Rectal tumor up to 12 cm from the external anal margin
5. Patients must be willing to comply with the study protocol and give their informed  written consent.
6. Patients with an ECOG status performance <3
Exclusion criteria:
1. Age less than 18 years
2. Previous cumulative dose of 250 mg/m2 of bleomycin exceeded;
3. Chronic renal dysfunction (creatinine> 150 µmol/L must be considered a lower  administered dose of bleomycin)
4. Pregnancy or lactation
5. Patients with neoplasia more than 12 cm from the anal margin
6. Patients with stable disease or disease progression after neoadjuvant treatment
7. Patients, who for medical reasons, cannot be given bleomycin
8. Lesions not suitable for ECT (bony invasion, large vessels infiltration, etc.);
9. Acute lung infection;
10. Symptoms of poor lung function;
11. Non correctable severe coagulation disorders;
12. Previous allergic reactions to bleomycin;
